# Trivy ignore list for go-signal.
#
# The gate is a SOURCE filesystem scan (trivy fs) of the module, failing on
# CRITICAL/HIGH (conventions/devops.md §8). test/ is the integration and
# performance harness; build/, bin/ and data/ are gitignored local artifacts.
# None of them ship.
#
# There is no image gate yet, and the reason is a broken build rather than an
# accepted risk: none of this repository's Dockerfiles build today. The
# top-level Dockerfile, Dockerfile.dev and Dockerfile.service still COPY from
# go-libsignal/go-xkms/go-qrdb/go-quicraft build contexts that only
# .devcontainer/docker-compose.yml supplies, and the deploy/Dockerfile.* build
# stage is golang:<stable>-alpine with no git, so `go mod download` cannot
# reach the first-party modules on Gitea. `make trivy-image` carries the
# ready-to-use scan loop over the six deploy/ service images; chain it into
# `make security` and add the CI job once the Dockerfiles build.
#
# Add specific advisory IDs below ONLY when a finding is confirmed
# not-applicable or unfixable, with a one-line justification AND the date it
# was accepted. An entry without both is a defect.
#
# Example:
# CVE-XXXX-XXXXX  # 2026-01-01 <reason this advisory does not apply to go-signal>
